esp32s31: the display stack, cumulative - PPA blend ioctl and RX-EOF completion

The four files below are wholly ours (they do not exist upstream), and the
patch series had fallen behind the 7.1 tree they live in: the PPA blend work
of 2026-08-30 existed only in the gitignored linux-71-port/. This patch is a
CUMULATIVE diff from the 6.12 BSP baseline (the linux-esp32-s31 submodule,
which scripts/port-kernel.sh carries into every fresh port tree) to the
current 7.1 state, verified byte-identical on reconstruction. For these four
files it SUPERSEDES the hunks in 0005/0006/0016/0017/0020 - on a fresh port,
copy the 6.12 files in and apply only this. (0006 set the precedent: these
snapshots overlap, they are not a quilt stack.)

New since 0020, previously unpreserved:

  * DRM_ESP32S31_PPA_BLEND: fixed-alpha two-layer blend in hardware, dst may
    equal bg for in-place compositing. Fill and SRM already had ioctls; blend
    was debugfs-only, so every compositor on this board blended in software.
  * An ARGB sprite blend path (per-pixel alpha source over an opaque
    background) - the one blend where nothing has to be made coherent twice.
  * PPA completion signalled by the 2D-DMA RX channel's IN_SUC_EOF, not the
    PPA's own EOF interrupt - IDF's dma2d callbacks do the same and none of
    them use the PPA interrupt. Waiting on the wrong bit cost 7.8x and skewed
    every PPA-vs-CPU decision made while it was wrong.
  * ppa_spin_us tuning notes: raising 300 -> 3000 only measured the sleep it
    replaced; the spin threshold stays at 300.

Deliberately NOT captured: the usbhid diagnostics in drivers/hid/usbhid/
(in-handler timing, short-report and io_error counters). They are
instrumentation, not product, and stay local to the working tree.

